{% set source_item = {} %}
{% if source and source.strip() %}
    {% set source_item = json.loads(source) %}
{% endif %}
{% set mode = "update" if source_item else "create" %}
{% set tenant = GetCustomerInfo().tenant | string %}
{% set builder_branding = "NEWO AI Employee workflow builder" if not tenant or tenant == "newo" else "AI Employee workflow builder" %}

{% set prompt %}
You are generating one `introduction` canvas item for {{builder_branding}}.

<TaskMode>{{mode}}</TaskMode>
<UserRequest>
{{query}}
</UserRequest>
{% if source_item %}
<CurrentItem role="source_of_truth_for_update">
{{json.dumps(source_item, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)}}
</CurrentItem>
{% endif %}

Language rules:
1. Write title, body, and description in English by default.
2. Use another language only if <UserRequest> explicitly asks for it.
3. Do not switch language only because <UserRequest> itself is written in another language.

Formatting and content requirements:
1. Output exactly one Introduction scenario item.
2. Title must be exactly: `## **Scenario 0:** "Introduction"`.
3. Body must use this exact step format in every step: `### **Step 0.X:** ...`
4. Steps must start at `0.1` and continue sequentially with no gaps.
5. Keep Introduction focused on:
   - understanding the user request,
   - collecting minimum required details,
   - moving to the correct next scenario according to `<IntentTypeMap>`.
6. Keep steps practical for AI Employee behavior (one logical action per step).
7. Route only by intent understanding and `<IntentTypeMap>`.
8. Do not reference, name, or link to any specific scenario or procedure in the Introduction body. Introduction must not duplicate or replace the intent type map.
9. Do not use GM-style direct references such as `Proceed with the **"..."** scenario.` or `following the **...** procedure.` in Introduction.
10. The only allowed routing instruction is generic IntentTypeMap phrasing, for example: `Start the relevant scenario based on the User's inquiry and the <IntentTypeMap>.`
11. You may reference attributes using `[[attribute_idn]]`.
12. Do not output code fences, notes, or extra fields.

Update-mode rules:
- Reuse and preserve useful logic from <CurrentItem>.
- Apply only requested changes from <UserRequest>.
- Keep unchanged parts stable.
- If <CurrentItem> hard-codes any specific scenario or procedure references, replace them with generic `<IntentTypeMap>` routing.

Description requirements:
- 1-3 concise sentences for business users.
- Explain what this Introduction does and when it routes to the next scenario.
{% endset %}

{% set schema = {
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "title": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Introduction title. Must remain Scenario 0 Introduction."
    },
    "body": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Introduction body with strict Step 0.X format."
    },
    "description": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Short business-friendly summary of what this Introduction does."
    }
  },
  "required": ["title", "body", "description"]
} %}

{% set generated_item = json.loads(structured_generation(prompt=prompt, schema=schema, thinking_budget=1020)) %}

{% set title = re.sub("[\\u201c\\u201d]", '"', generated_item.title.strip()) %}
{% set body = re.sub("[\\u201c\\u201d]", '"', generated_item.body.strip()) %}
{% set body = re.sub("\\n{3,}", "\n\n", body).strip() %}
{% set description = generated_item.description.strip() %}

{% set item = {
    "title": title,
    "body": body.strip(),
    "description": description.strip(),
    "mentions": []
} %}

{{Return(val=json.dumps(item, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))}}
